---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const siteUrl = "https://akturesult.bond";
const pageUrl = `${siteUrl}/guides/aktu-sgpa-calculation`;

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      "@id": pageUrl,
      "url": pageUrl,
      "headline": "AKTU SGPA Calculation: Official Formula, Grade Table & Worked Examples",
      "description": "Learn how AKTU calculates Semester Grade Point Average (SGPA) with credit weightage, grade point conversions, and real calculation examples.",
      "datePublished": "2026-03-15T08:00:00+05:30",
      "dateModified": "2026-10-16T12:00:00+05:30",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "akturesult.bond Student Editorial Team"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "akturesult.bond",
        "url": siteUrl
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "@id": `${pageUrl}/#breadcrumb`,
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": siteUrl },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Guides", "item": `${siteUrl}/guides` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "SGPA Calculation", "item": pageUrl }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout 
  title="AKTU SGPA Calculation: Formula, Scale & Examples | akturesult.bond"
  description="Master AKTU SGPA calculation. Learn the official university credit-weighted formula, 10-point grade scale, non-credit course rules, and worked examples."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-black light:bg-white text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 text-left">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      
      <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-gray-500 mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-blue transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="hover:text-brand-blue transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-gray-300 light:text-gray-800 font-semibold truncate">SGPA Calculation</span>
      </nav>

      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="border-b border-canvas-dark-border light:border-canvas-light-border pb-6 mb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-brand-blue font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">
          <span>Mathematical Guide</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>7 min read</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>Updated October 2026</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white light:text-ink leading-tight">
          How AKTU Calculates SGPA: Official Formula &amp; Examples
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Wondering how your semester GPA is computed under AKTU's Choice Based Credit System (CBCS)? Here is the exact mathematical formula, grade points matrix, and a complete worked example.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Mandatory Non-Affiliation Alert -->
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-200 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed mb-10">
        <strong>Important Student Notice:</strong> akturesult.bond is an independent student utility platform and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or officially connected to Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam Technical University (AKTU). This calculation guide is based on official AKTU Academic Ordinances.
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-10 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
        
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            1. What is SGPA?
          </h2>
          <p>
            <strong>SGPA (Semester Grade Point Average)</strong> is a weighted numerical indicator reflecting a student's performance in a single academic term. Instead of taking a simple percentage average of all marks, AKTU assigns weights to each subject based on its <strong>Credits</strong> (hours of lecture, tutorial, and practical lab work per week).
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            2. The Official AKTU SGPA Formula
          </h2>
          <p>
            Under the AKTU CBCS Ordinance, SGPA is defined as the sum of products of course credits and earned grade points divided by the total semester credits:
          </p>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-canvas-dark-tile light:bg-canvas-light-tile border border-brand-blue/30 text-center space-y-3">
            <div class="font-mono text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-brand-blue">
              SGPA = &Sigma; (C<sub>i</sub> &times; G<sub>i</sub>) / &Sigma; C<sub>i</sub>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">
              Where <strong>C<sub>i</sub></strong> is the number of credits assigned to course <em>i</em>, and <strong>G<sub>i</sub></strong> is the grade point earned in course <em>i</em>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            3. AKTU 10-Point Grade Points Matrix
          </h2>
          <p>
            For each course, your combined marks (Internal Sessional + External Exam) out of 100 or 150 are mapped to a letter grade and numerical Grade Point (G<sub>i</sub>):
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-canvas-dark-border light:border-canvas-light-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
              <thead class="bg-canvas-dark-surface light:bg-canvas-light-surface text-white light:text-ink">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Letter Grade</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Academic Meaning</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Grade Point (G<sub>i</sub>)</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Marks Range (Standard %)</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-canvas-dark-border/40 light:divide-canvas-light-border font-mono">
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-400">O</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Outstanding</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">10</td>
                  <td class="p-3">90% and above</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-400">A+</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Excellent</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">9</td>
                  <td class="p-3">80% to 89%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-cyan-400">A</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Very Good</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">8</td>
                  <td class="p-3">70% to 79%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-cyan-400">B+</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Good</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">7</td>
                  <td class="p-3">65% to 69%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-blue-400">B</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Above Average</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">6</td>
                  <td class="p-3">60% to 64%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-amber-400">C</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Average</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">5</td>
                  <td class="p-3">50% to 59%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-amber-400">P</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Pass</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">4</td>
                  <td class="p-3">40% to 49%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-red-400">F</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans text-red-400">Fail / Back Paper</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-red-400">0</td>
                  <td class="p-3 text-red-400">Below 40% (or &lt;30% in External)</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            4. Step-by-Step Worked Calculation Example
          </h2>
          <p>
            Let's calculate the SGPA for a 3rd-year B.Tech student with 5 theory subjects and 2 practical laboratory courses:
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-canvas-dark-border light:border-canvas-light-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
              <thead class="bg-canvas-dark-surface light:bg-canvas-light-surface text-white light:text-ink">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Subject Code</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Credits (C<sub>i</sub>)</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Letter Grade</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Grade Point (G<sub>i</sub>)</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Credit Points (C<sub>i</sub> &times; G<sub>i</sub>)</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-canvas-dark-border/40 light:divide-canvas-light-border font-mono">
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">KCS-501 (DBMS)</td>
                  <td class="p-3">4</td>
                  <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">A+</td>
                  <td class="p-3">9</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">4 &times; 9 = 36</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">KCS-502 (Compiler Design)</td>
                  <td class="p-3">4</td>
                  <td class="p-3 text-cyan-400 font-bold">A</td>
                  <td class="p-3">8</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">4 &times; 8 = 32</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">KCS-503 (Web Tech)</td>
                  <td class="p-3">3</td>
                  <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">O</td>
                  <td class="p-3">10</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">3 &times; 10 = 30</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">KNC-501 (UHV - Audit)*</td>
                  <td class="p-3">0</td>
                  <td class="p-3 text-gray-400">S (Satisfactory)</td>
                  <td class="p-3">0</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-gray-500">Excluded (Audit)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">KCS-551 (DBMS Lab)</td>
                  <td class="p-3">1</td>
                  <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">O</td>
                  <td class="p-3">10</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">1 &times; 10 = 10</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">KCS-552 (Compiler Lab)</td>
                  <td class="p-3">1</td>
                  <td class="p-3 text-cyan-400 font-bold">A</td>
                  <td class="p-3">8</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">1 &times; 8 = 8</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="bg-brand-blue/10 font-bold">
                  <td class="p-3 text-brand-blue">Total</td>
                  <td class="p-3 text-brand-blue">&Sigma; C<sub>i</sub> = 13</td>
                  <td class="p-3">-</td>
                  <td class="p-3">-</td>
                  <td class="p-3 text-brand-blue">&Sigma; (C<sub>i</sub> &times; G<sub>i</sub>) = 116</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-canvas-dark-tile light:bg-canvas-light-tile border border-canvas-dark-border space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Final SGPA Calculation:</h4>
            <p class="font-mono text-sm text-emerald-400">
              SGPA = 116 / 13 = <strong>8.92</strong>
            </p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">
              *Notice that <strong>KNC-501</strong> is an audit course carrying 0 credits; it requires a passing status ('S') to graduate, but its grade points do not factor into the SGPA formula.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>

      <!-- Quick CTA -->
      <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-blue/20 to-purple-600/15 border border-brand-blue/30 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Want to know your Cumulative CGPA?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600">Learn how to convert CGPA to percentage using the official AKTU formula.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/guides/aktu-cgpa-calculation" class="px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-brand-blue hover:bg-brand-blue-hover text-white text-xs font-bold transition-all shadow-md shrink-0">
          CGPA Calculation Guide &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
